{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"5bf529795931a029","name":"card_unit_katzmann","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_katzmann","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"KATZMANN REGIMENT","text":"Increase operation cost by 1 until end of turn each time you play another card.","flavorText":"Regiment Katzmann was a short-lived formation within the rebuilt German 84th Infantry Division. The division had first gone to France with only two grenadier regiments, 1051 and 1052, a weakness typical of the 25th deployment wave raised from Ersatzheer (literally Replacement Army) manpower in 1944. The 84th Infantry Division had been deployed in February 1944 and fought in France during Operation Overlord. Its first formation was destroyed on 20 August in the Falaise Pocket. It was reformed near Kleve with a third regiment. This new unit was first known as Katzmann, but on 24 December 1944 it received the formal designation Regiment 1062. The rebuilt division then faced the Western Allies on the lower Rhine. It was again destroyed at the Wesel bridgehead during Operation Varsity in 1945. A further rebuilding was planned in the Lüneburg Heath, but the war ended before it could take shape.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_katzmann","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_katzmann_title","SourceString":"KATZMANN REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"KATZMANN REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_katzmann_text","SourceString":"Increase operation cost by 1 until end of turn each time you play another card.","LocalizedString":"Increase operation cost by 1 until end of turn each time you play another card."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_katzmann_history","SourceString":"Regiment Katzmann was a short-lived formation within the rebuilt German 84th Infantry Division. The division had first gone to France with only two grenadier regiments, 1051 and 1052, a weakness typical of the 25th deployment wave raised from Ersatzheer (literally Replacement Army) manpower in 1944. The 84th Infantry Division had been deployed in February 1944 and fought in France during Operation Overlord. Its first formation was destroyed on 20 August in the Falaise Pocket. It was reformed near Kleve with a third regiment. This new unit was first known as Katzmann, but on 24 December 1944 it received the formal designation Regiment 1062. The rebuilt division then faced the Western Allies on the lower Rhine. It was again destroyed at the Wesel bridgehead during Operation Varsity in 1945. A further rebuilding was planned in the Lüneburg Heath, but the war ended before it could take shape.","LocalizedString":"Regiment Katzmann was a short-lived formation within the rebuilt German 84th Infantry Division. The division had first gone to France with only two grenadier regiments, 1051 and 1052, a weakness typical of the 25th deployment wave raised from Ersatzheer (literally Replacement Army) manpower in 1944. The 84th Infantry Division had been deployed in February 1944 and fought in France during Operation Overlord. Its first formation was destroyed on 20 August in the Falaise Pocket. It was reformed near Kleve with a third regiment. This new unit was first known as Katzmann, but on 24 December 1944 it received the formal designation Regiment 1062. The rebuilt division then faced the Western Allies on the lower Rhine. It was again destroyed at the Wesel bridgehead during Operation Varsity in 1945. A further rebuilding was planned in the Lüneburg Heath, but the war ended before it could take shape."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunct